WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.380
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.340
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:09.940
Thus far on Aikatsu!

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.460
My name is Hoshimiya Ichigo, and my family runs a bento shop.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.200
I turned my scoop into a mic and became an idol.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.290
A year has passed, and it's time for the super duper huge annual event to decide the Academy's top idol.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.170
The Starlight Queen Cup is upon us!

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.170
In a twist of fate, the Cup's opening concert

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.920
was none other than the 
legendary idol unit Masquerade.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:39.060
After Masquerade disbanded, Miya disappeared from the public eye and hasn't been heard from since.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.430
There's something I'd like to talk about.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:45.270
That I've turned my mic into a scoop.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.040
Mama?!

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.360
<i>Dear Aikatsu fans around the globe,</i>

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:01.620
<i>I, Hoshimiya Raichi, have stumbled upon an unbelievable truth after watching Masquerade's performance on TV.</i>

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:08.470
<i>There wasn't just one, but two idols' scents in my house!</i>

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:48.100
Headmistress Orihime.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.850
The doctor has an update on Mizuki's condition.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.170
Excuse me, did something happen to Mizuki-san?

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.730
She collapsed before her concert.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.630
Don't worry, she'll be fine.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:01.720
But...

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.010
Mama?!

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.620
I did the opposite of what you did.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.880
I turned my mic into a scoop.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:15.810
But Mama...

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.420
Why are you dressed like Miya-chan from Masquerade?

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:24.260
Aoi, Ran...

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:26.780
We just happened to hear you through the door...

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:29.290
But really, are you serious?

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.660
Is it really true?

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.610
Is what true?

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.330
You two burst in here at exactly the right time.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.900
No wonder you're all in a unit.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.550
Thank you very much.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.660
Miya-chan praised us!

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:45.600
Of course.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.950
By "Miya-chan"...

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.670
What? You're in Masquerade?!

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:53.920
Yeah!

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.480
What?!

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.610
Mama, you were in Masquerade?

00:03:58.610 --> 00:03:59.050
Yeah.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.740
And you were Miya-chan?

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:01.390
Yep.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:03.000
You were in a unit with Hime-chan?

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:03.380
Uh-huh.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.490
And Hime-chan is Headmistress Orihime?

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:06.000
That's right.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.870
Then that means you used to be an idol before you opened the bento shop?

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:09.600
Exactly.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.550
And you were an idol in Masquerade?

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:12.110
Yeah.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:13.890
And you were Miya-chan?

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:14.480
Yep.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.640
She's going in circles.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.190
You can't take your eyes off these two for a second.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.190
Yes?

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:25.320
So you called yourself "Miya-chan" because of the "Miya" in "Hoshimiya"?

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.620
Bingo!

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.330
Excellent concert today,

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.830
Hime-san.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.330
It's been quite a few years since the last time you called me that.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:39.210
That's because today's me is acting as Masquerade's choreographer.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:45.220
That concert was amazing and fantastic and woo!

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:46.340
But...

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.760
But, but, but!

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.350
<i>Here it comes.</i>

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.840
If I were to give you one point of advice,

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:58.770
it would be better if you stopped your right hand more crisply during the first step.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:04.610
And one more thing: the way your swung to the rhythm after that was sweet.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:08.770
<i></i>This<i> is the fabled Johnny-style criticism.</i>

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:13.990
<i>He starts out by praising what you did well, but follows up with an endless stream of detailed constructive criticism.</i>

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:18.630
<i>It's a professional technique that's guaranteed to improve your overall performance.</i>

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.880
If you keep all of that in mind, your next concert will be even more amazing.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:28.390
Whenever I take your comments to heart, my next performance always goes better.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.260
Yeah!

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:32.250
But I'm afraid you've wasted your breath.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.870
Masquerade's revival was for one night only.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:38.030
The time when Miya and I could stand on stage together is already...

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:39.360
Over? {ehh}

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.740
Though I won't let you say it.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:42.480
What?

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:45.370
The public's response was enormous.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:48.740
An uncountable number of fans rejoiced at your comeback.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.010
Did you really think...

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:54.000
we'd let you off with just one performance?

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:59.500
Man, that was surprising.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.500
If I were to try and compare my surprise to something...

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.550
It would about the same as if I opened a seaweed bento only to find curry inside!

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:07.880
That would leave even me speechless.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:09.150
Right?

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.960
Ichigo hasn't changed.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:12.760
Yeah.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:17.520
Even though her mom kept being an idol a secret, Ichigo isn't the least bit angry.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.750
Anyway, I'm a lot more concerned about Mizuki-san right now.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:21.520
Me too.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:25.780
It's hard to believe that she was able to pull off that concert right after collapsing.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.760
The concert was so striking that I still can't believe it.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:33.490
Mizuki-san really is the toughest idol out there.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:40.330
I'm fine now, they gave me an IV drip and everything.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:43.280
Regardless, I want you to rest well today.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:48.210
During the Starlight Queen Cup, you'll be facing whoever comes out on top

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:51.220
in a final concert for the title.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:54.230
Right, I need to rest and gather my strength.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:57.200
Yes, of course.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.260
I was thinking how much I wanted to do so as well.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:02.450
Got it. See you then.

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:04.860
I'm ready now!

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:07.750
Alright then, I'll be back home tomorrow.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:08.600
Sure.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.580
So you're already calling this school your home.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.090
Take it easy back home.

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.120
It's your last chance to relax before the Cup.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.900
I will. Headmistress Orihime 
said the same thing too.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:24.080
Mama and I will talk about all sorts of things together.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.030
It's Hoshimiya Ichigo!

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:27.800
Ran-chan's there too!

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.800
Aoi-chan!

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.190
Thanks for coming!

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:36.860
Huh? It doesn't seem like anyone's figured out that you're in Masquerade.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:41.850
Only when I'm wearing a mask am I a true idol.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:43.850
We're home!

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:48.300
W-Welcome back.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:52.570
Why are you so stiff, Raichi?

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.950
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.330
It's still only a hypothesis anyway.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:59.110
Hypothesis?

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.200
<i>I realized something while watching Masquerade's concert.</i>

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:12.760
<i>Miya-chan's aura had the faint scent of Mom.</i>

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.760
<i>Is it just my imagination?</i>

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:17.140
<i>I know!</i>

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:25.700
Raichi, do you need something?

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.100
Not really...

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.530
<i>I-Isn't this...</i>

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.300
<i>Oh wow, oh wow, oh wow, oh wow... {this really doesn't look good without punctuation, does it...}</i>

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:45.540
<i>I'm ready!</i>

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.300
Onee-chan.

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:50.750
What's up?

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:53.300
I stumbled upon something incredible.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:54.470
What's that?

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.930
W-Well... the truth is...

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.680
M-Mom is—

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.570
Onee-chan, you already knew that Mom was Miya-chan?

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:10.960
Yeah.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:15.410
How could you leave me out of the loop...

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.870
Thanks for dinner!

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.120
I'm sorry, Raichi.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.120
I was going to tell you everything after we ate dinner.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:26.750
Don't worry, I'm not mad.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:30.620
But to think we had two idols in this house!

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:34.630
So Mama, why did you originally want to become an idol?

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:39.010
Ever since I was a little girl, I loved to sing and dance.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:45.390
I always sang and practiced with my friends up on the stage in the park.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.360
And that friend was Hime-chan?

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:48.640
Not quite.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:52.850
One day, a different friend told me about an open audition.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.280
And<i> that</i> was Hime-chan?

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.280
No, but the girl I met at the audition...

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:58.700
Was Hime-chan!

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.530
Right.

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:04.610
Once I realized how much I loved making other people happy with my music,

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:08.790
I decided to become an idol and take an audition.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.290
On my way there...

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.070
Is this a mask?

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:21.050
It is...

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:24.030
a mask. {ugh}

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:27.560
That was my first encounter with Hime.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:33.510
Her voice was so beautiful that I couldn't help but join in next to her.

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:43.920
Both of us went on to pass our respective auditions.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:52.380
Wait, Ringo!

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:54.130
Let's form a unit!

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:06.640
From then on I began to wear a mask as well, and we eventually made our debut.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:12.680
There were just so many amazing things that happened during my time in Masquerade.

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:15.950
I bet Aoi would kill to hear your stories.

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:20.030
Oh, don't worry about that. Aoi-neesan and I have an information network set up already.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:23.340
Idol fans walk a path where collaboration is key.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:25.780
You recorded the whole thing?

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:30.540
Looks like Aoi was right.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:35.090
She told me that Raichi had the potential to reach the highest levels of idol fandom.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:37.120
I wouldn't doubt that.

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:41.210
He even realized that you were in Masquerade all on his own.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.110
Ichigo, just so you know,

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:48.580
the reason that I never told you I was an idol...

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:49.730
I know.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:55.480
It was because you wanted me to make my own decisions about becoming an idol, right?

00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:02.990
The reason I became an idol was because of that dazzling concert that Mizuki-san put on,

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:06.570
not to mention because of Aoi inviting me to attend Starlight Academy.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.880
It's also because of your support,

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:12.960
and because of Ran, and Otome-chan,

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:16.000
Yurika-chan, and Sakura-chan too—

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.720
It was because of Kaede-chan, and Headmistress Orihime,

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:20.780
and also...

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:23.510
Right, and because of Johnny-sensei too.

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.760
I couldn't have done it without everyone's help.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:30.550
But if it wasn't my decision in the first place, I may have given up halfway.

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:31.520
Exactly.

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:36.200
Your decision wasn't based on 
something like me being an idol.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:39.160
I wanted you to forge your own path through life.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:44.660
There's someone who once told me the very same thing.

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:48.150
Want to come see her with me tomorrow?

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:49.750
I really need to thank her again.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:50.540
Sure.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:54.830
Then tomorrow we'll do Aikatsu together.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:11.640
I never would've expected that you also personally knew Amane-san from Angely Sugar.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:17.400
Even though she had a lot of work as a Top Designer, she still had the time to teach me all sorts of things.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.150
About Angely Sugar,

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:24.650
about how to coordinate outfits, and about the spirit of Aikatsu.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:28.660
I often came here to ask her for advice.

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:37.600
Oh well. Back in my day, there wasn't even an elevator anyway.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.590
To make our way to Asuka-san's house...

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:40.830
Yep, I know.

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:42.670
Let's climb!

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:44.920
Yeah!

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:53.180
Ai... katsu...

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.200
I love this.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:59.440
Having to use your own hands and feet, your own strength to scale this cliff. {SO DANGEROUS}

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:03.690
Your own strength alone determines how far you can climb.

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.000
It's exactly like the idol world as a whole.

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:09.160
Your own strength...

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:13.000
That's one of the things Asuka-san taught me.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.330
Alright!

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:24.210
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:32.470
Aikatsu... Aikatsu...

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:36.230
Ai... katsu!

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:39.230
Ai...katsu!

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:51.470
Thanks.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:58.210
I've been waiting for the day you two would come here together.

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:02.630
When I decided to quit being an idol and follow my dream of running a bento shop,

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:05.470
Asuka-san was the one who helped guide me the most.

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:06.590
Really?

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:10.220
I really loved being an idol,

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:14.280
but as I gazed upon the smiles of my fans from up on stage,

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:17.130
I got the urge to know each of them personally.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.810
As I stood there thinking that,

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:27.190
I suddenly remembered my childhood dream of opening a bento shop.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:31.860
I wanted to speak with them face to face, to share our happiness—

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.200
Becoming an idol only strengthened my ambition.

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:39.060
While I was deep in thought, Asuka-san told me that I had a certain talent.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:42.970
Do you mean talent as an idol, or as a shop owner?

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:43.920
Not quite.

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:48.950
It was the talent to feel exactly what I needed to do to become happy.

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:52.970
She told me that if there was something I really wanted to do, I should go ahead and do it.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:58.220
The only person who can understand what makes you happy is yourself.

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:01.810
That was one of the lessons that Asuka-san taught me.

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:06.350
It was right around that time that Hime got the offer to become the Academy's headmistress.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:09.760
The two of us had a long talk...

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:12.740
many long talks, in fact...

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.320
Until we decided to disband.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:19.240
I want you to treasure your 
happiness as well, Ichigo-chan.

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:21.310
I will!

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:24.250
Asuka-san, thank you once again.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.000
I'm very happy right now. {I'm very happy you didn't use "blissful"}

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:30.180
So am I.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:32.880
That's right.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.390
There's something I'd like you to see, Ichigo-chan.

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:39.390
It's a new Premium Dress.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:43.890
The Star Festival Coord. Do you like it?

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:48.980
It's super pretty!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.360
It's sparkling just like the rice at home.

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.860
When it's been cooked for just the right time.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:58.480
I was watching the concert where you wore the Starlight Tiara

00:16:58.480 --> 00:17:01.790
and got the urge to make you this outfit to go along with it.

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:04.670
Ichigo-chan, will you wear it for me?

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:07.540
Of course! Thank you so much.

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:19.820
Here you are.

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:22.400
Thank you.

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:25.010
To performers, cards are life itself.

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:28.940
They are the foundation all idols build their careers on.

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:32.800
It's the same with a hairstylist's scissors, {or serial killer}

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:35.480
or a tennis player's racket.

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:38.910
In the end, the most important thing is...

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:41.200
Yourself, right?

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:42.950
Precisely.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:47.920
I've made plans to hold one more concert alongside Hime.

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:50.000
Huh, you have?

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:53.710
Asuka-san, would you come watch us?

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:56.090
I'd love to.

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:03.360
This really will be our final concert as the reborn Masquerade. {or "Masquerade Reborn"}

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:04.220
Right.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:07.700
Once we step off stage, I'll go back to being a headmistress.

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:10.210
And I'll return to my bento shop.

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.230
Let's have fun out there.

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:12.710
Yeah!

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:10.480
Thank you, Hime.

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:15.370
And thank you, too. I'll call Ichigo-chan later and tell her how it went.

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:18.630
Hime-san, Miya-san.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:19.850
Mizuki?

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:24.380
I'm very sorry for the trouble I caused you a few days ago.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:27.080
That's fine, but are you feeling better?

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:29.010
Yes, thanks to you.

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:32.620
I have something to tell you, Mizuki-chan.

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:33.970
I know.

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:39.270
Ichigo-chan resembles you very much, Miya-san.

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:44.960
Seems like Ichigo-chan's got a clever senpai of her own.

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:48.780
I'd like to thank you, Mizuki-chan.

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:52.810
It's because of you that Ichigo can shine as brightly as she does.

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:56.010
I was simply the spark that set her aflame.

00:21:57.520 --> 00:21:59.040
I'm home!

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:01.000
Good to see you, Ichigo!

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.180
Did you have fun going back home for... a while?

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:06.800
More than you can imagine!

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:08.800
I brought you back some food.

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:12.310
Try some.

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:15.440
At the time, we had yet to realize

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:21.310
that each of us was already walking down the paths to our own futures.

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:57.700
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.860 --> 00:24:01.140
Do you prefer mountain cliffs or sea cliffs?

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:03.990
Sea cliffs! They come up a lot in police dramas too.

00:24:03.990 --> 00:24:07.940
I like mountains! Matterhorn is my favorite one of all!

00:24:07.940 --> 00:24:09.840
Idols love cliffs.

00:24:10.520 --> 00:24:13.040
Oh man, the Starlight Queen Cup!

00:24:13.040 --> 00:24:14.350
It's finally starting!

00:24:14.350 --> 00:24:16.450
First up is a battle between us seven.

00:24:16.450 --> 00:24:18.640
Let's make this the best concert ever!

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:20.180
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:20.180 --> 00:24:21.770
Where the brilliance leads us.

00:24:21.770 --> 00:24:25.830
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
